    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d421">

                <pb facs="0657" n="555" sameAs="frus:frus1935v01/pg555"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.90H/23</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Straus</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1282</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1934-10-13">October 13,
                        1934</date>.<lb/>[Received October 23.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to report that on the
                    occasion of the call which the Afghan Minister, H. R. H. Shah Wali paid on me,
                    after my communication to him of September 6, 1934,<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d421-f1"/> enclosing, in accordance with the Department’s
                    Instruction No. 549 of August 28, 1934,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d421-f2"/> the
                    original and copy of a letter addressed by the President to His Majesty Mohammed
                    Zahir, King of Afghanistan, according the recognition by the United States of
                    Afghanistan, H. R. H. Shah Wali raised the question of future relations between
                    the Afghan monarchy and the United States. He expressed the hope that these
                    relations might be established on a permanent basis as soon as possible and that
                    to that end a treaty of friendship should be concluded. He followed up this
                    suggestion by a note, a copy and translation of which are enclosed
                        herewith.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d421-f3"/>
                </p>
                <p>In my reply, a copy and translation of which are likewise transmitted
                        herewith,<anchor n="3" xml:id="d421-f4"/> I contented myself with saying
                    that I had carefully examined his communication and would not fail to take up
                    the matter with him at a later date. Since that reply, I have had a personal
                    talk with H. R. H. Shah Wali on the occasion of M. Barthou’s<anchor n="4"
                        xml:id="d421-f5"/> funeral, at which time I informed him that I had
                    forwarded his letter to the Department of State. Accordingly, I shall await the
                    Department’s suggestions for a reply.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Jesse Isidor Straus</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
